Hellproof patch 0003 over stwo_cairo_verifier@cd7bc5f — fri_answers with lazy numerators and
one batch inversion of all denominators (verifier_core/src/pcs/quotients.cairo).

Invariant: for every query row, answer = -(sum over batches of reduce(a_b*y + b_b -
sum over columns of c_{b,col} * v_col) * den_b^-1) with the batches, coefficients
(QuotientConstantsImpl::gen) and denominators (fused_quotient_denominator) of the original code.

Why equivalent: (1) gen stores its sums and coefficients reduced (the packed sums are offset by
large_zero() before the reduction, as a packed lane of mul_cm31 may have borrowed across 2^128 —
the original absorbed it by adding the offset alpha_mul_b_sum before its single reduce); (2) the
numerators are accumulated per sample point on four unreduced felt252 limbs, offset by P * 2^41
above the negative column terms; batches of different degree-bound groups sampled at the same
point (the OODS point, the previous point, the periodicity batch of the largest columns sampled
at the OODS point) are summed before the multiplication by their common inverse denominator — a
reassociation of a ring sum; (3) the denominators are the same formula, inverted through their
norms ((a + bi)^-1 = (a - bi)/(a^2 + b^2), what the vendored CM31 inverse computes) with one
batch inversion of all the proof's norms; (4) the row sum over the classes is formed on unreduced
limbs (products below 2^135, offset P * 2^105, sum below 2^141 < 2^248), reduced once and
negated. Row-by-row equality with the unmodified verifier is asserted by
crates/stwo_circuit_phases/tests/test_equivalence.cairo. Details: vendor/patches/README.md.

